<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ejisu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ejisu is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> region of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>. Its queen mother, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaa-asantewaa">Yaa Asantewaa</a>, led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-golden-stool">War of the Golden Stool</a> against the British in 1900, the last major armed resistance of the Ashanti Empire against colonial rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ejisu.jpg" alt="Ejisu" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joy Agyepong · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ejisu_Bebease_Shrine_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The final act of resistance came in 1900, when Yaa Asantewaa, Queen Mother of <b>Ejisu</b>, led the War of the Golden Stool, one of the last major armed risings against British rule in West Africa, after Governor Sir Frederic Hodgson demanded that the Golden Stool be surrendered to…</blockquote><a href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1900, after the king’s exile, Yaa Asantewaa, queen mother of <b>Ejisu</b>, led the War of the Golden Stool against the British.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ashanti">Social Hierarchy of the Ashanti Empire</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1900 the governor's demand for the Golden Stool, the sacred symbol of the Asante nation, provoked a rising led by Yaa Asantewaa, queen mother of <b>Ejisu</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/ashanti-colony">Ashanti Colony</a></li></ul></section>
